    <briefdescription>
<para>This struct provides a method for customizing the way a cast is performed. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It inherits from <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_is_possible" kindref="compound">CastIsPossible</ref>, to support the case of declaring many <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_is_possible" kindref="compound">CastIsPossible</ref> specializations without having to specialize the full <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info" kindref="compound">CastInfo</ref>.</para>
<para>In order to specialize different behaviors, specify different functions in your <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info" kindref="compound">CastInfo</ref> specialization. For isa&lt;&gt; customization, provide:</para>
<para><computeroutput>static bool isPossible(const From &amp;f)</computeroutput></para>
<para>For cast&lt;&gt; customization, provide:</para>
<para><computeroutput>static To doCast(const From &amp;f)</computeroutput></para>
<para>For dyn_cast&lt;&gt; and the *_if_present&lt;&gt; variants&apos; customization, provide:</para>
<para><computeroutput>static To <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info_1a09597b5e97eabe6d1cc60e6846a989a3" kindref="member">castFailed()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput>static To doCastIfPossible(const From &amp;f)</computeroutput></para>
<para>Your specialization might look something like this:</para>
<para>template&lt;&gt; struct <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info" kindref="compound">CastInfo&lt;foo, bar&gt;</ref> : public <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_is_possible" kindref="compound">CastIsPossible&lt;foo, bar&gt;</ref> { static inline foo doCast(const bar &amp;b) { return foo(const_cast&lt;bar &amp;&gt;(b)); } static inline foo <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info_1a09597b5e97eabe6d1cc60e6846a989a3" kindref="member">castFailed()</ref> { return foo(); } static inline foo doCastIfPossible(const bar &amp;b) { if (!CastInfo&lt;foo, bar&gt;::isPossible(b)) return <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info_1a09597b5e97eabe6d1cc60e6846a989a3" kindref="member">castFailed()</ref>; return doCast(b); } }; </para>
    </detaileddescription>
